  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run, NOT merged, no status change). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/surar (worktree ~/hg_wt/surar), local commit d5e987abce \"fix(ruby): a constant receiver's module slot is the constant as written (WI-surar)\". Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/surar.md.\n\nCHANGE: ruby.py _try_receiver_call constant-external fallback now sets module_hint = receiver_class.lstrip(\":\") -- the constant as written, less a root \"::\" (Net::HTTP, File, JSON, Rack::Utils). The require-hint lookup and the .lower() heuristic are gone from this path (the require hint is a last-segment-keyed FILE hint; it still serves bare-call and base-class resolution); the now-unused require_hints parameter of _try_receiver_call is removed. The two project-owner producers in the same function already used the as-written spelling. call_construct stays \"method\" (the ADR-0059 function-kind question is not touched).\n\nBEHAVIOUR (verify-claims, overlay net_recv row get, fixture \"require 'net/http'; def fetch(u) X.get(URI(u)) end\", must_not_exist claim):\n  origin/dev: row Net::HTTP, call Net::HTTP -> inconclusive (the filed defect)\n  branch:     row Net::HTTP, call Net::HTTP -> violated; rows net/http and HTTP -> violated (pinned)\n  branch:     row Net::HTTP, call Faraday::HTTP -> inconclusive (namespace control); a mutant that drops the namespace but keeps case turns it violated, so the control can fail.\nTESTS: test_ruby_constant_receiver.py +14 cases (red on origin/dev: 9 failed); targeted smart-test on the branch: 10235 passed, 1 skipped, 4 xfailed, 0 failed, changed source files 100% covered. Five tests that pinned the old spelling were corrected to the analyzer's output (test_ruby x2, polyglot ruby fixture, core test_io_overlay_uncatalogued_language, core test_verify_claims).\n\nMEASURED (analyze_ruby, origin/dev vs branch, by call site): postal/chatwoot/mastodon edge totals and constant-external site sets identical (474/1844/2539 sites); slots: case-only 291/1520/2065, namespace restored 180/322/465, require path 3/2/9. On mastodon 3 sites were WRONG before (RSpec::Matchers attributed to paperclip/matchers via a last-segment require hint). Spelling change only: no catalogue, no boundary count moves.\n\nNOT DONE / NOT CLAIMED: the general claim \"every ruby module slot is an owner path\" is not asserted -- only the constant-receiver fallback was changed. A constant that names a VALUE (postal's Postal::Config = initialize_config, 125 sites) gets that constant, not the value's type. Instance receivers on external types emit no edge at all (pre-existing, separate). Filed: WI-gomup (lexical constant lookup misses compact class A::B declarations, seen on chatwoot), WI-mahik (perl's sibling: Pkg->m emits no edge / binds receiver-blind)."  # eba6
