  message: "DONE: merged in PR #1383. _try_receiver_call uses the constant as written minus a leading :: as the module slot: Net::HTTP.get -> ruby:Net::HTTP:0-0:get with or without require 'net/http'; File.write -> File. Behavioural evidence: verify-claims with an overlay net_recv {module: Net::HTTP, functions: [get]} over Net::HTTP.get: inconclusive on dev, violated on the branch; a Net::HTTP row leaves Faraday::HTTP.get inconclusive, and a namespace-dropping mutant turns that control violated (pinned in test_ruby_constant_receiver.py through verify-claims). Corpus (postal / chatwoot / mastodon, per call site): identical edge and call-site sets; 180 / 322 / 465 slots regained their namespace; 3 mastodon sites lost a wrong paperclip/matchers attribution. NOT asserted: every Ruby module slot is an owner path (Postal::Config = runtime value gets the constant's name). Residuals: WI-gomup, WI-mahik (P2).\nFull report (closure evidence, corpus tables, residual list): /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/surar.md"  # 4405
